    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that, but isn't that kind of a worst-case scenario though? like, most people would probably be fine with it if it actually prevented a major terrorist attack or found a kidnapper. it feels like the \"social control\" argument is a bit of a stretch and doesn't really account for the practical benefits of actually making cities safer for everyone.",
