      "content": "The \"worst-case scenario\" is precisely why the technology is so dangerous, as unchecked power always trends toward misuse. While preventing a terrorist attack is a noble goal, that benefit does not grant a government the right to build a permanent, pervasive surveillance state over its population. The practical benefit of safety is a weak justification when weighed against the fundamental right to anonymity in public life.",
